From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: rsinput: wait for the params ack, reset on a retry, init off the resume path

The MCU init sent the parameter command (which selects framed reports)
and returned success without waiting for its acknowledgement, so a lost
params command left a dead or free-running pad that nothing retried.
Wait for the DATA_COMMOD_SET_PAR reply (or the first status report:
the reports are what the params are for) as the version request
already is, and start over when either is missing. The wait window is
now under a spinlock, so a late reply to one request cannot complete
the next, and a CMD_COMMOD frame without a payload is not read as one.

A retry did not reset anything: the AYN boards have no reset line and
the power-on sequence only ever raised enable. Drop enable for the
100 ms settle so each attempt power-cycles the MCU.

A handshake failure at probe failed probe for good, while resume
retried from a work; probe now hands a slow MCU to the same retries.
Resume no longer powers the MCU up synchronously (100 ms plus its
boot, up to ~3 s): the work does it.

The boot/enable/reset GPIO lookups only warned on error, leaving an
ERR_PTR that every later gpiod call ignored; an error (a deferral above
all) now fails probe.

Status reports: every report holds the whole button state, so report
all of it and let the input core pass on the changes, instead of a
function-static previous state that went stale when the core released
the keys across suspend (a button held through sleep never showed as
pressed again). The triggers are clamped to the range reported for
them; a reading past the rest position is 0, not a negative value.

A rumble stop goes through while rumble_enable is off, so turning it off
mid-effect cannot leave the motor running; the never-created sysfs
attribute is gone (the module parameter remains). rsinput_rx() already
checks each frame, so it dispatches directly instead of reparsing it,
and the ABS ranges are set by one helper.
---
